# title: Shark fin note
# category: Barriers and touch options
# underlyings: 1
# source: Rubinstein & Reiner, Breaking Down the Barriers, Risk, 1991
# source: Bouzoubaa & Osseiran, Exotic Options and Hybrids: A Guide to Structuring, Pricing and Trading, Wiley, 2010
# summary: A capital-protected note paying the stock's rise, unless the stock ever closes at or above the barrier: then only a rebate on top of the capital.
# param: notional = 1000 | amount | Notional
# param: participation = 1.0 | percent | Participation in the rise
# param: barrier = 1.25 | percent | Knock-out barrier, % of the initial level
# param: rebate = 0.05 | percent | Rebate if knocked out, % of notional
#
# Capital protected at maturity; daily closes. Its payoff chart looks like a
# shark's fin: rising, then a cliff.

2027-01-04
    notional = 1000
    participation = 1.0
    barrier = 1.25
    rebate = 0.05
    s0 = spot()
    alive = 1

schedule(2027-01-05, 2027-12-30, 1D, US, F)
    if spot() >= barrier * s0 then alive = 0 endIf

2028-01-04
    if spot() >= barrier * s0 then alive = 0 endIf
    if alive = 1 then
        pays notional * (1 + participation * max(spot() / s0 - 1, 0))
    else
        pays notional * (1 + rebate)
    endIf
